# Files verified apart (separate cpp-verify runs, or clang++ compiling each
# object) record the contracts they verify and those they assume from other
# files; --check-contracts settles them together, as one run over the files
# does, and fails for each proof whose assumed contract is not established.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --contracts-out=%t/a.json %S/Inputs/across/src/a.cpp \
# RUN:   -- -I%S/Inputs/across/include 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=APART --implicit-check-not=warning:
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --contracts-out=%t/wrong.json %S/Inputs/across/src/mathx.cpp \
# RUN:   -- -I%S/Inputs/across/include -DBUG=101 > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --contracts-out=%t/right.json %S/Inputs/across/src/mathx.cpp \
# RUN:   -- -I%S/Inputs/across/include -DBUG=100 > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --check-contracts %t/a.json %t/wrong.json 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRONG
# RUN: %cpp-verify --check-contracts %t/a.json %t/right.json 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RIGHT
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --check-contracts %t/a.json 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MISSING
#
# Through the compiler, each object's record beside it.
# RUN: %clang -std=c++17 -fverify-contracts -Rcppverify -fverify-contracts-out=%t/a.o.cppverify \
# RUN:   -c %S/Inputs/across/src/a.cpp -o %t/a.o -I%S/Inputs/across/include 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REMARK
# RUN: %clang -std=c++17 -fverify-contracts -Rcppverify -fverify-contracts-out=%t/m.o.cppverify \
# RUN:   -c %S/Inputs/across/src/mathx.cpp -o %t/m.o -I%S/Inputs/across/include -DBUG=100
# RUN: %cpp-verify --check-contracts %t/a.o.cppverify %t/m.o.cppverify 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RIGHT
# RUN: not %clang -std=c++17 -fverify-contracts -fverify-contracts-out=%t/w.o.cppverify \
# RUN:   -c %S/Inputs/across/src/mathx.cpp -o %t/w.o -I%S/Inputs/across/include -DBUG=101 > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --check-contracts %t/a.o.cppverify %t/w.o.cppverify 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRONG
#
# Contracts whose proofs rest on each other establish nothing.
# RUN: %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --contracts-out=%t/ping.json %S/Inputs/across/src/ping.cpp -- > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %cpp-verify --jobs=1 --contracts-out=%t/pong.json %S/Inputs/across/src/pong.cpp -- > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --check-contracts %t/ping.json %t/pong.json 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CYCLE
#
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --check-contracts %S/Inputs/across/src/a.cpp 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOT-RECORD
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --contracts-out=%t/both.json %S/Inputs/across/src/a.cpp \
# RUN:   %S/Inputs/across/src/mathx.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SEVERAL

A proof that rests on a contract of another file says so.
APART: Verified: scaled [backend=z3] [assumes=clamp100]
APART-NEXT: Verified: twice_scaled [backend=z3] [assumes=clamp100]

Through the compiler each proof is a remark at its function.
REMARK: a.cpp:3:5: remark: Verified: scaled [backend=z3] [assumes=clamp100] [-Rcppverify]
REMARK: a.cpp:9:5: remark: Verified: twice_scaled [backend=z3] [assumes=clamp100] [-Rcppverify]

WRONG: a.cpp:3:5: error: the proof of scaled relies on the contract of clamp100, which its verification in {{.*}}mathx.cpp does not establish
WRONG-NEXT: a.cpp:9:5: error: the proof of twice_scaled relies on the contract of clamp100, which its verification in {{.*}}mathx.cpp does not establish
WRONG-NEXT: Contracts: 2 proofs rest on contracts of other files, 2 on one not established

RIGHT: Contracts: 2 proofs rest on contracts of other files, 0 on one not established

MISSING: a.cpp:3:5: error: the proof of scaled relies on the contract of clamp100 (no definition; mark it {{\[\[cppverify::trusted\]\]}} to assume it), which is not established

CYCLE: ping.cpp:5:5: error: the proof of ping relies on the contract of pong, whose proof in {{.*}}pong.cpp rests in turn on contracts not established
CYCLE-NEXT: pong.cpp:5:5: error: the proof of pong relies on the contract of ping, whose proof in {{.*}}ping.cpp rests in turn on contracts not established

NOT-RECORD: error: {{.*}}a.cpp is not a contracts record (cppverify.contracts/1)

SEVERAL: error: --contracts-out records one file; a run over several files settles their contracts itself
